type rates.", "observed_result": ["[APPS-080] Gate: C1 8/8 p<0.05; C2 S=0.319 perm_p=0.0002; C3 R2=0.080 PASS. Full: frobenius P1a S=0.352 p=0.0000 CI[0.327,0.378]; P1b S=0.353 CI[0.329,0.379]; cosine P1a 0.155 / P1b 0.144. residual_R2=0.043. D_obs mean=3 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[CHT-049] Residual R^2=0.043. Frobenius P1a S=0.352 p=0.0000 CI [0.327, 0.378]; P1b S=0.353 [0.329, 0.379]. Cosine P1a S=0.155 [0.132, 0.179]; P1b S=0.144 [0.123, 0.170]. All p<0.01."], "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "[CHT-049] NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-PAP-001"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-001", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-001: A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "score": 0.844, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-001", "FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-001"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "If the A1 adapter PPP lift is real coverage response, wrong-way teams should do worse than no-signal teams, the gap should widen with scheme-vote confidence, and adapting in Game N should carry over to Game N+1.", "observed_result": "T1 dPPP: adapter +0.0667 (n=205), neutral +0.0248 (n=50), no_signal +0.1260 (n=57), wrong_way +0.0111 (n=274). T2: adapter minus no-signal -0.0361 (1 vote), -0.1170 (2 votes). T3 next-game PPP Welch t=-1.003, p=0.842; MW [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node"